(2745840, 380057, 51750, '<td valign="top">Im really surprised that this ribboned, i dont like the expressionless face at all. This picture also apears to be totaly static to me when in reality it should not be at all. And last of all a little tiny fire extinguisher???<br/> <br/>So imo i think that the fact that theres a partially naked girl in the photo infuenced people to vote it higher.</td>', 'Im really surprised that this ribboned, i dont like the expressionless face at all. This picture also apears to be totaly static to me when in reality it should not be at all. And last of all a little tiny fire extinguisher??? So imo i think that the fact that theres a partially naked girl in the photo infuenced people to vote it higher.', '2006-08-21 11:55:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2745857, 380017, 50641, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  I knew I was in for trouble. I''m not crazy about them naked dnmc comments but ultimately, they still tell me what the viewer is thinking, to some limited extent. It''s funny, though, that red burny things don''t get the benefit of the doubt in a fire challenge ;-)</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  I knew I was in for trouble. I''m not crazy about them naked dnmc comments but ultimately, they still tell me what the viewer is thinking, to some limited extent. It''s funny, though, that red burny things don''t get the benefit of the doubt in a fire challenge ;-)', '2006-08-21 12:03:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2745860, 380057, 33068, '<td valign="top">Glad to see this type of shot in the top three.  Very well executed.  Going into favs.</td>', 'Glad to see this type of shot in the top three.  Very well executed.  Going into favs.', '2006-08-21 12:05:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2745913, 379928, 43031, '<td valign="top">Hey Judi, I saw your thread and decided to comment. First off, didn''t vote, so I''m not going to compare this to anything but for it''s own sake.<br/> <br/>I''ll play ''devils advocate'' (bwahahahahaha, I kill me!) ahem.<br/> <br/>Personally, I hate the title. But being a religious guy, you have to realize that Satan actually means something more to me than to others, and is not to be used lightly (by me. I only say that because I think others may consider this also, so it would be important to consider when entering here is all.<br/> <br/>Be that as it may, I think you might have gotten too engrossed in the concept here and ignored some details. It''s not a bad concept by any means, I think theres too much room around you, especially over your head to give impact. If the fire was still bigger and there were more swirling and dynamic patterns in the smoke this may have worked better with this framing. Should have been tighter  cropped or framed IMO. The lighting is really great as always with you. I think having the smoke in front of you somewhat distracts the eyes and deadens some of the impact. <br/> <br/>It''s not "bad alien porn" (stupid comment IMO) but It''s probably the least "tasteful" of your the more racey shots that you''ve done (not that I''ve seen everything I guess). I think this may be because some of the others were more a study of the human form, and this does seem more overtly sexual to me at least. I think it was on the edge of the line for some people. Maybe if you had the leather pants on instead of the leather panties? :P</td>', 'Hey Judi, I saw your thread and decided to comment. First off, didn''t vote, so I''m not going to compare this to anything but for it''s own sake. I''ll play ''devils advocate'' (bwahahahahaha, I kill me!) ahem. Personally, I hate the title. But being a religious guy, you have to realize that Satan actually means something more to me than to others, and is not to be used lightly (by me. I only say that because I think others may consider this also, so it would be important to consider when entering here is all. Be that as it may, I think you might have gotten too engrossed in the concept here and ignored some details. It''s not a bad concept by any means, I think theres too much room around you, especially over your head to give impact. If the fire was still bigger and there were more swirling and dynamic patterns in the smoke this may have worked better with this framing. Should have been tighter  cropped or framed IMO. The lighting is really great as always with you. I think having the smoke in front of you somewhat distracts the eyes and deadens some of the impact.  It''s not "bad alien porn" (stupid comment IMO) but It''s probably the least "tasteful" of your the more racey shots that you''ve done (not that I''ve seen everything I guess). I think this may be because some of the others were more a study of the human form, and this does seem more overtly sexual to me at least. I think it was on the edge of the line for some people. Maybe if you had the leather pants on instead of the leather panties? :P', '2006-08-21 12:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2746009, 379440, 49007, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm... The first thing I notice when I look at this is the fuzzy halo caused by the blurring of the background. I think you over did it with the blur and your selection control needs a bit of work. For example look at her fingertips. They came out slightly fuzzy.<br/> <br/>Just my personal preference, but since it''s advanced I would have touched up the stray hairs by cloning.<br/> <br/>I like the composition, except I''d like to see more of her expression (blocked by the hair) and the face of the girl in the background.</td>', 'Hmmmm... The first thing I notice when I look at this is the fuzzy halo caused by the blurring of the background. I think you over did it with the blur and your selection control needs a bit of work. For example look at her fingertips. They came out slightly fuzzy. Just my personal preference, but since it''s advanced I would have touched up the stray hairs by cloning. I like the composition, except I''d like to see more of her expression (blocked by the hair) and the face of the girl in the background.', '2006-08-21 12:57:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2746042, 380057, 60899, '<td valign="top">Toooo goood...........lot of work put into it</td>', 'Toooo goood...........lot of work put into it', '2006-08-21 13:15:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2746045, 379927, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Larus:</b></div><hr/><i> I just gotta ask, why the f20 and iso 800?  Why not iso 200 and f10, wouldn´t that have lead to better image quality?  Eh who cares, you still beat my ass so maybe I should try those settings too next time :P  Congrats on the honorable mention, looks like you guys beat us this week :( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think the best answer I can give you Lárus is the photo itself and the results in the challenge. But in fact I did take several shots this evening with different settings, but this one had the right grainy appearance I was trying to achieve.</td>', 'Originally posted by Larus: I just gotta ask, why the f20 and iso 800?  Why not iso 200 and f10, wouldn´t that have lead to better image quality?  Eh who cares, you still beat my ass so maybe I should try those settings too next time :P  Congrats on the honorable mention, looks like you guys beat us this week :(   I think the best answer I can give you Lárus is the photo itself and the results in the challenge. But in fact I did take several shots this evening with different settings, but this one had the right grainy appearance I was trying to achieve.', '2006-08-21 13:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2746050, 380057, 16053, '<td valign="top">Caro Jorge: parabéns pela excelente fotografia e a mestria no controlo da luz. É sempre com grande satisfação que vejo um fotógrafo português se distinguir dos demais pela sua qualidade, grande qualidade do seu caso. Espero que as suas excelentes fotos sejam uma fonte de inspiração para os colegas fotógrafos portugueses para que estes se rendam ao dpchallenge para que qualquer dia possamos fazer um encontro de dpc''s em portugal.<br/> <br/>Por ''ultipo resta-me apenas acrescentar um agradecimento pela explicação de como a fotografia foi tirada e da pós produção da mesma. Esse é um assunto com o qual eu tenho-me sempre debatido quer aqui no dpchallenge que em outros locais do género, pois para quem quer aprender trata-se de uma grande fornte de aprendizagem e mostra o espírito de abertura do fotógrafo.<br/> <br/>Best regards and the wish of many future ribbons.</td>', 'Caro Jorge: parabéns pela excelente fotografia e a mestria no controlo da luz. É sempre com grande satisfação que vejo um fotógrafo português se distinguir dos demais pela sua qualidade, grande qualidade do seu caso. Espero que as suas excelentes fotos sejam uma fonte de inspiração para os colegas fotógrafos portugueses para que estes se rendam ao dpchallenge para que qualquer dia possamos fazer um encontro de dpc''s em portugal. Por ''ultipo resta-me apenas acrescentar um agradecimento pela explicação de como a fotografia foi tirada e da pós produção da mesma. Esse é um assunto com o qual eu tenho-me sempre debatido quer aqui no dpchallenge que em outros locais do género, pois para quem quer aprender trata-se de uma grande fornte de aprendizagem e mostra o espírito de abertura do fotógrafo. Best regards and the wish of many future ribbons.', '2006-08-21 13:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2746088, 380057, 62187, '<td valign="top">After consulting with the experts, I''d like to add that just because I don''t care for the results nor subject - I feel compelled to add that I have no problems with the photographic quality of your image.</td>', 'After consulting with the experts, I''d like to add that just because I don''t care for the results nor subject - I feel compelled to add that I have no problems with the photographic quality of your image.', '2006-08-21 13:38:29.000000', NULL, 0),
